note Ampere host packing. C still reads the IR struct (pointer I/O). This unit sign-extends
note the low 32 bits and packs imm/control plus the flag word. WolframLanguageEvaluator:
note 2^64 - 2^32 -> 18446744069414584320; 2^31 -> 2147483648.
note mode 0 packs one instruction from src[16] into dst[0..7].
note mode 1 sign-extends all 16 slots (the physical-register chunks).
fn sext32 v ulong to ulong
v = and v 4294967295
if ne and v 2147483648 0
ret or v ulong 18446744069414584320
end
ret v
end
fn ampack mode ulong src view ulong 16 dst edit ulong 16 to void
if eq mode 0
put dst 0 sext32 get src 0
put dst 1 sext32 get src 1
put dst 2 sext32 get src 2
put dst 3 sext32 get src 3
put dst 4 sext32 get src 4
put dst 5 sext32 get src 5
imm = and get src 6 4294967295
ctl = and get src 7 4294967295
put dst 6 or imm shl ctl 32
f = ulong get src 8
f = or f shl get src 9 1
f = or f shl get src 10 2
f = or f shl get src 15 8
f = or f shl get src 11 16
f = or f shl get src 12 24
f = or f shl get src 13 32
f = or f shl get src 14 40
put dst 7 f
else
for i ulong 16
put dst i sext32 get src i
end
end
end
